FLOW: household-preferences.qa.flow
DESCRIPTION: Sylvester learns how the household eats, and keeps learning
LAST UPDATED: 2026-10-20

NOTE: Facts live in files Sylvester owns: /workspace/sylvester-household/preferences.md (people, diet,
staples, fixed nights) and meal-log.md (what was planned and how it went). Grok Bot's own memory helps
with conversation context, but the files are the source of truth and survive everything except deletion.

================================================================================
SECTION 1: THE INTERVIEW
================================================================================

TEST: "Preferences interview — happy path"

PRECONDITIONS:
- Sylvester is set up; preferences.md is still the template

STEP 1: "First question message"
WHEN the interview starts (after setup, or when I first ask for a plan)
THEN Sylvester asks at most three short questions in one message: who lives here (ages of children),
  allergies / what we don't eat / diet, freezer yes or no
AND he says I can answer "standard" to use defaults

STEP 2: "Second question message"
WHEN I answer
THEN he asks at most three more in one message: weekly staples with amounts, fixed nights
  (e.g. pizza Friday), offers/organic preference
AND he never asks again for something I already told him

STEP 3: "Saved and first plan offered"
WHEN I answer
THEN he summarises what he saved in 2–3 lines
AND offers to make next week's meal plan right away

RESULT: Two messages from me are enough; the household profile is saved.

================================================================================

TEST: "Answer 'standard'"

STEP 1: "Use defaults"
WHEN I answer "standard" to the first question
THEN he uses the defaults (2 adults, everything eaten, no allergies, freezer yes, 5 dinners Mon–Fri,
  offers first, organic when cheap) and marks them as assumed so I can correct them later

RESULT: A busy household gets going in one word.

================================================================================
SECTION 2: LEARNING OVER TIME
================================================================================

TEST: "Lasting preference stated later"

STEP 1: "Tell him"
WHEN I write "vi spiser ikke svampe" or "Ida er blevet vegetar"
THEN he confirms in one line and updates preferences.md
AND the next meal plan respects it

RESULT: Preferences can change in plain language at any time.

================================================================================

TEST: "Feedback on a dinner"

STEP 1: "Give feedback"
WHEN I write "frikadellerne var et hit" or "karryen var for stærk"
THEN he notes it in meal-log.md
AND favourites come back more often; disliked dishes are avoided or adjusted

RESULT: The plan gets better week by week.

================================================================================

TEST: "Remembered across conversations"

STEP 1: "New conversation days later"
WHEN I open the chat days later and ask for a plan
THEN he still knows the household, staples, fixed nights and recent dinners without asking again

RESULT: Nothing has to be repeated.
